  "notes": [
    "Whisper model used: 'small' (CLI, fp16=False, language=es) for ref-08..ref-13. ref-03..ref-06 transcriptions were pre-existing — they were generated with an unknown Whisper model/config (size impacts WPM precision by 2-5%).",
    "Pace section split: hook=0-15% / dilemmas=15-80% / outro=80-100% of total duration. Empirical mapping (not from spec).",
    "LUFS per section computed via ffmpeg ebur128 over short windows — values for sections <3s are noisy and reported as-is.",
    "Music BPM = librosa.beat.beat_track on mixed audio (narration + music + SFX). Use as approximation; true musical BPM may differ when narration dominates.",
    "Visual analysis uses 18-21 frames extracted at ~5s intervals by the original pipeline (frame_*.jpg). NOT frame-by-frame — represents key-moment sampling.",
    "dominant_hue_deg uses 12 buckets of 30°. Label maps: red(0-30) / orange(30-60) / yellow(60-90) / yellow-green(90-120) / green(120-150) / teal(150-180) / cyan(180-210) / blue-cyan(210-240) / blue(240-270) / purple(270-300) / magenta(300-330) / pink-red(330-360).",
    "vignette_ratio: <1.0 = darker center than edges (rare); 1.0 = flat; >1.0 = brighter center, classic vignette. Typical cinematic = 1.05-1.20.",
    "grain_variance: 25th-percentile of 16x16 block variances in center region. Higher = more film grain texture. Compare across refs to gauge consistency.",
    "ref-03..ref-06 silences_count in metadata.json appears to use a high noise threshold — silences.txt parsing may yield slightly different counts.",
    "vignette_ratio >1.0 here means CENTER is brighter than EDGES (which is the opposite of the classical 'vignette' label). For vertical reels with centered subjects, ratio 1.3-1.5 is typical = subject highlighting + edge darkening = strong vignette / soft vignette in classical sense. Lower ratio (1.0-1.15) = flat lighting.",
    "dynamic_range_db is p95-p5 of frame RMS in dBFS (robust to silence floor). Higher = more variation between loud peaks and quiet sections. Typical music with ducking 10-25 dB.",
    "rms_db_outro reads very low (-25 to -37 dB avg) for several refs — they have a closing 'punchline' / cliffhanger zone with reduced energy. Don't read this as 'audio bug'; it's a deliberate creative pattern.",
    "Aggregated visual.dominant_hue_deg is omitted because it averages a circular variable and the result is meaningless. Use visual.dominant_hue_distribution (categorical histogram) instead.",
    "pacing.cuts_per_min uses DE-CLUSTERED counts (cuts within 0.5s collapsed to one — closer to perceptual scene changes). pacing.cuts_per_min_raw shows the raw ffmpeg detection count including flash/glitch clusters. ref-13 raw=31.7/min vs declustered=5.1/min — the raw count was inflated by 8 flash bursts.",
    "pacing.flash_bursts = count of detection clusters of >=3 cuts within <0.5s. Indicates flash transitions / glitch effects / rapid montage moments. Many F1 refs have 0-3; ref-13 has 8."
  ],
